Object.assign(DIALOG_CLIPS.clips,{"amy|TOM. Oh, thank goodness.":"","grace|Ran off? Like, RAN? On legs?":"","amy|The bells ring whenever they feel like it. Every clock says a different time. And the sign-up sheet ran off.":"","michael|Mrs. Gregori! Thank goodness. And you brought the whole family.":"","tom|Hello. I hear your bells are haunted.":"","michael|Not haunted. Grumpy. Thirty-one years in this building. I know the difference.":"","michael|The bells ring at random. The clocks in the hall all say different times. And the sign-up sheet got up off the table and walked into the school.":"","michael|Set every clock in the hall to seven. Seven o’clock. Not seven-thirty. Not six-fifty-nine. Seven.":"","tom|Stay close, everybody. This is a professional learning environment.":"","rose|Tata. A school. At NIGHT. With MONSTERS, probably.":"","tom|...Every clock in this hall says a different time.":"","rose|Tata! Tata! SPARKLY FOOTPRINTS!":"","amy|That one says four. That one says nine. That one is going BACKWARDS. I teach time, Tom. This is personal.":"","rose|Little paper feet. With glitter. They go EVERYWHERE.":"","grace|The footprints go into all three. Then out again. Then east, to the Cafetorium.":"","grace|I can read the doors. Room One is ART. Room Two is MUSIC. Room Three is the GYM.":"","tom|Then we clear Art, Music and the Gym. After each one, we fix its clock. Seven o’clock.":"","rose|Rhubarb crisp! Deedee brings the teachers CRISP?":"","amy|She never told me that. Of course she never told me that.":"","tom|To the moon and back. And apparently to the staff room.":"","log|...DING. Prove it.":"","amy|Up! Everybody up! Walk it off. Hydrate. We go again.":"","grace|Tata, listen. The clock outside the Art room stopped spinning.":"","rose|The glitter footprints stop here! And over there. And on Tata.":"","toad|BOING. Everybody against the wall. Nobody picks me first. Nobody EVER picks me first.":"","amy|Oh, I remember you. Fourth grade. You and me. Every Friday.":"","tom|Amy was the scariest kid in dodgeball. They had to make a rule about her.":"","amy|You caught the pie, though.":"","tom|I know. You threw one at me at Thanksgiving. I was holding a pie.":"","tom|I caught the pie.":"","amy|The footprints go in there. The sign-up sheet is in there.":"","grace|And the something.":"","grace|There! The sign-up sheet! On the podium!":"","grump|Click. Wrong. Wrong. Wrong. Every name on this sheet is written wrong.":"","grump|Kowalski has a W. Delgado has a G. Gregori has TWO Rs, and nobody ever writes them neatly.":"","tom|You took the sign-up sheet to grade it.":"","grump|Nobody ever grades ME. Nobody ever writes NEAT next to ME. So tonight, I grade the grown-ups.":"","grump|And the bells. And the clocks. Late is late. Points off.":"","amy|I have used a thousand pens like you. Put the sheet down. Now.":"","amy|Up. Everybody. Walk it off.":"","amy|Tom, when it says SEE ME, step in front of them. Grace, Squishy anyone it circles. And somebody tell it its handwriting is nice. Three times.":"","tom|A gold coin. Again. Same little clock face.":"","tom|We keep it. In my pocket. Not inside Lamby.":"","michael|The sheet! The bells! The clocks! Parents, come on in! Conference night is ON!":"","michael|Mrs. Gregori. Best conference night in thirty-one years. Not one parent cried. Well. Mr. Delgado. Happy tears.":"","amy|Thirty conferences. Zero tears. One very well-behaved pen.":"","amy|Oh. A text. From Justin.":"","grace|Dad used the heart! He only uses the heart on special days!":"","amy|\"Heard it went great. Proud of you. Stuck at work till nine. Save me a cookie.\" With a little heart.":"","amy|Girls. Did we save a cookie for Dad?":"","rose|...Define save.":"","tom|...Nobody there.":"","tom|Probably.":"","tom|By default.":"","amy|Everybody in the van. Tom, you too. You were the good uncle tonight. By a lot.":"","amy|By a LOT. Take the compliment, Tom.":"","dot|Ten doors and THREE gaps in the trees now. Somebody opened one by the school.":"","michael|Come to Field Day, Tom. Amy runs the relay. Amy always runs the relay.":"","michael|Thirty parents. Zero tears. One very well-behaved pen. Best conference night in thirty-one years.":"","michael|Conferences start at seven. SEVEN. The bells say otherwise. The bells are wrong.":"","michael|Clear the rooms, set the hallway clocks to seven, and the Cafetorium will open. I hope.":"","bean|Marco is reading at a third-grade level! Mrs. Gregori showed me the chart. There was a chart!":"","oolong|Thirty conferences, nine hundred cookies, one laminator. Everything went on schedule. MY schedule.":"","oolong|Kowalski. PTA president. I brought nine hundred cookies and a laminator.":"","gus|The bells were wrong in 1956 too. Nobody fixed them. Things were simpler.":"","amy|Thirty conferences. Zero tears. Well. One. Mine. In the minivan.":"","skeeter|I have nine questions and one of them is a trick.":"","skeeter|Retake! Pencils up!":"","skeeter|Round 2. Question 2. Show your work.":"","skeeter|Round 3. Question 3. Show your work.":"","skeeter|Round 4. Question 4. Show your work.":"","skeeter|Round 5. Question 5. Show your work.":"","skeeter|The answer is C. The answer is always C.":"","log|Ding ding! Round two!":"","log|Everybody groans when I ring. Every single time. For forty years.":"","log|Round 2. You are late for round 2.":"","log|Round 4. You are late for round 4.":"","log|Round 3. You are late for round 3.":"","log|Round 5. You are late for round 5.":"","log|...Ding. Quietly. Ding.":"","log|I ring on time. Everybody else is late.":"","mudling|Still sticky!":"","mudling|Kids use me for one art project and then I sit in a drawer for three years.":"","mudling|Round 2. Even stickier.":"","mudling|Round 4. Even stickier.":"","mudling|Round 3. Even stickier.":"","mudling|Round 5. Even stickier.":"","toad|Back in the game!":"","toad|I just want to be picked first. Once.":"","toad|Round 2. Still not picked.":"","toad|Round 3. Still not picked.":"","toad|Round 4. Still not picked.":"","toad|Round 5. Still not picked.":"","toad|Nobody picks me. They just throw me.":"","grump|Retake! From the top!":"","grump|A hundred thousand wrong answers. I marked every single one.":"","grump|Neatness counts. Nobody counts it. I count it.":"","grump|Round 2. Still a C minus.":"","grump|Round 3. Still a C minus.":"","grump|Round 4. Still a C minus.":"","grump|Round 5. Still a C minus.":"","grump|...Points off. Points off for everybody.":"","grump|Nobody gets a hundred. NOBODY.":"","deedee|Not tonight, honey. I made a plate for the teachers. Somebody has to keep Boppy away from it.":"","boppy|A school? At night? My stomach says no. My knees say absolutely not.":"","amy|Pick up the pace, Tom. The girls are faster than you.":"","sal|Long Island Elementary is east of the Square. Follow the clipboard.":"","amy|Rose, shoes. Grace, water. Tom, posture.":""});
